{
  "about": "Solana nodes as templates the brain enforces for each relay vault (solguard::template, contracts/brain/src/sol.rs): every instruction is checked byte by byte before the vault signs. Accounts: 'vault' is the vault itself, 'vault_ata' its own token account for the mint at position mint_at (re-derived, so proceeds can't go anywhere else), 'new_signer' a fresh key (a new LP position), 'fixed' a pinned address, 'any' an account the program itself checks against the others (pool PDAs, bin arrays). Trailing extra accounts are never signers. needs_owner: the owner's own Solana wallet must co-sign (set with sol_owner_wallet). Values in {braces} are set per coin by the owner and filled in when the template is saved. vault_ata_of is the vault's own token account for a fixed mint the instruction doesn't name (wrapping SOL). Tested on a Solana mainnet fork (surfpool) on 2026-11-06: contracts/sandbox/tests/sol_fork.rs (pump.fun buy + sell), sol_fork_meteora.rs (DLMM open/add/claim/remove/close), sol_fork_pumpamm.rs (pump AMM buy + sell of a graduated coin, with wSOL wrap/unwrap).",
